  "published": "2026-08-27T02:49:44.22Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Checkpoints. The 0.1.0 README claimed the arena was position-independent and that\ncheckpointing cost a file write, without an API to do it. Now there is one.\n\n- Snapshot writes a set of arenas and named roots to a stream and reads them back.\n  The file is the blocks verbatim: no traversal, no pointer fixup. A Handle written\n  down before the save is the same value after the load, and points at the same node.\n- AddSet, AddList, AddTree and AddHandle pull in the arenas they need. AddTree adds\n  two of them, because a RedBlackTree keeps its nodes in Arena<ArenaList<T>>\n  and its values in Arena<T>.\n- ArenaState<T> is an arena's state as an object; Arena<T>.Capture, Restore\n  and Swap move it around. The storage stays static, so the hot path is unchanged.\n- Where it loses: the file weighs the reserved capacity rather than the live keys;\n  every checkpoint is the whole arena, with no incremental writes and no compression;\n  T must hold no references; and a file only loads on the same byte order and the\n  same node layout. All of it is in the README.\n\n68 tests, up from 42. No breaking changes.",
